# Request explicit maintainer review for review-control changes.
#
# **The owner is the public organisation, not a personal handle.** This file used to
# name `@bensenescu` on every line — the account owner's personal identity, published
# in a file every contributor reads, for no benefit a code-owner rule cannot get from
# the organisation itself. The control is identical: an entry with no owner requests
# no review at all, so it has to be owned, and the organisation is the owner that
# does not publish an individual.
#
# Two other things fell out of this file when the private repo became a sibling of
# this one:
#
#   `.greptile/`, `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and `.agents/skills/` are no longer in this
#   repository — they moved to the private repo, which holds its own harness rules. An
#   entry for a path that is not here is dead weight, and worse: it reads as though the
#   file still exists somewhere above this line's directory.
#
#   `/.agents/plugins/` was removed as duplicated subject matter. Its own comment
#   already explained that the plugin root ships to every installed user, which is the
#   same claim `/plugins/` makes, so one rule covers both.
/.github/ @RatioArtificiosa

# Plugin distribution — these files define the MCP endpoint and skills every plugin
# installer connects to; a silent change here ships to all installed users on the next
# update.
/plugins/ @RatioArtificiosa
/.claude-plugin/ @RatioArtificiosa
/.agents/plugins/ @RatioArtificiosa
